{%- comment -%}
  Wig Party — child items for one mega-menu link.

  Shopify navigation supports one level of nesting and the mega menu honours it rather than
  flattening it. Extracted into its own snippet so the divided and padded list renderers
  share one copy instead of each carrying a duplicate nested loop.

  Titles and URLs come straight from the menu — nothing here is hardcoded, so a merchant
  adding or removing a child item in Admin → Content → Menus changes the panel with no code
  change.

  Params: link — a `linklists[...].links` item that has `link.links`
{%- endcomment -%}
<ul class="aria-mega__sublinks" role="list">
  {%- for child in link.links -%}
    <li>
      <a
        href="{{ child.url }}"
        class="aria-mega__sublink"
        {% if child.current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
      >{{ child.title }}</a>
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
</ul>
